Antigravity Execution Plan — Fast.com-Style Speed Test Engine
Goal

Upgrade the existing Speedometer project from a single-server LibreSpeed-style test into a Fast.com-inspired distributed speed-testing architecture.

Primary objectives
Keep the existing Next.js UI and design.
Replace the current simplistic measurement behavior.
Use multiple geographically distributed test servers.
Automatically select the best server.
Use adaptive parallel download streams.
Measure sustained throughput instead of short bursts.
Add accurate latency, jitter, upload, and download testing.
Prevent cached or artificially inflated results.
Support failover when a server becomes unavailable.
Phase 1 — Repository Audit and Architecture Preparation
Objective

Understand the existing implementation before replacing the measurement engine.

Tasks
Audit the current speed-test engine.
Identify:
Server configuration.
Current LibreSpeed integration.
Download logic.
Upload logic.
Ping and jitter logic.
Result calculation.
Identify all environment variables.
Identify frontend components connected to the test engine.
Preserve the existing UI contract.
Create clear separation between:
UI.
Test orchestration.
Server discovery.
Network measurement.
Result calculation.
Required rule

Do not modify the existing UI design unless required for functionality.

