Execution Order

Antigravity should implement this strictly in phases:

Phase 1  → Audit current engine
Phase 2  → Refactor architecture
Phase 3  → Build server registry
Phase 4  → Add server probing
Phase 5  → Implement server selection
Phase 6  → Implement adaptive downloads
Phase 7  → Implement throughput sampling
Phase 8  → Implement stable result calculation
Phase 9  → Implement upload testing
Phase 10 → Implement latency/jitter
Phase 11 → Add test state machine
Phase 12 → Connect existing UI
Phase 13 → Improve backend endpoints
Phase 14 → Deploy distributed infrastructure
Phase 15 → Add failover
Phase 16 → Add abuse protection
Phase 17 → Test against real services
Final Success Criteria

The completed system must:

Keep the existing UI unchanged.
Use real network measurements.
Select the best available server.
Support multiple geographic servers.
Use adaptive parallel connections.
Measure sustained throughput.
Support accurate ping and jitter.
Support upload testing.
Handle server failures automatically.
Avoid short-term speed spikes as final results.
Produce results that are reasonably comparable to Fast.com, while not claiming to reproduce Netflix's proprietary infrastructure or methodology exactly.